<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime">
    <!--
        Ambient Accent Visual System — spacing/geometry tokens (D-1). xmlns:sys targets
        "System.Runtime", not the "mscorlib" the docs/Refactoring/UI/*.xaml draft used: this project is
        net8.0-windows, and mscorlib type-forwarding for System.Double is not a markup-compiler contract
        worth relying on (D-1 pitfall #1). Declared on the dictionary root, not per-element.

        Panel-specific layout constants (header height, accent indicator thickness, header button size)
        deliberately do NOT live here — they live in Models/PanelMetrics.cs (C2) as C# constants consumed
        via x:Static, so there is exactly one source of truth per value instead of a XAML copy that could
        drift out of sync with the C# one (the exact failure mode D-11 calls out for TitleBarHeight before
        this phase).
    -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.2">2</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.4">4</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.6">6</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.8">8</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.10">10</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.12">12</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.16">16</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="Space.24">24</sys:Double>

    <!--
        Radius.Control/Radius.Popup are UNCHANGED from Phase 5 (3/4 respectively) — this pass
        (docs/PLANS/workspace-grid-07-visual.md "Border radius") only widens Radius.Panel, and only after
        adding an explicit clip (Converters/RoundedRectClipConverter.cs, Resources/Styles/Panels.xaml's
        PART_Chrome) so square-cornered content can no longer poke past the rounded corner — the risk
        Phase 5's own comment here used to cite as the reason NOT to touch this token ("no DoD calls for
        a radius change... unreviewed visual regression risk"). That DoD now exists (P07-visual) and the
        clipping precondition it named is met, so this token moves.

        Radius.Panel: 6 -> 8. 8 DIP is exactly one ADR-028 workspace-grid unit (WorkspaceGridMetrics.UnitSize)
        — not because this token is PART of that grid (it explicitly is not: ADR-028 states the workspace
        grid and icon-layout grid are "namely incommensurable" systems, and this is a third, purely
        cosmetic geometry with no snapping semantics at all), but because it is a convenient, already-
        load-bearing round number in this codebase to reuse rather than inventing an arbitrary new one.
        Safety margins checked before picking it: 8 is a quarter of PanelMetrics.HeaderHeight (32) — the
        header's own title/icon/button row still reads as a normal rectangular strip, not an
        exaggerated "pill" — and under a sixteenth of WorkspaceGridMetrics.MinWidthSpanExpanded (96 DIP,
        ADR-028's floor for an expanded panel's width) and PanelMetrics's own hard 120 DIP WPF-floor
        (GridMetrics.MinPanelSize) — even the smallest allowed panel has ample straight edge left on
        every side. Manual verify: docs/PLANS/workspace-grid-07-visual.md's DPI/wallpaper review pass.
    -->
    <CornerRadius x:Key="Radius.Panel">8</CornerRadius>
    <CornerRadius x:Key="Radius.Control">3</CornerRadius>
    <CornerRadius x:Key="Radius.Popup">4</CornerRadius>

    <Thickness x:Key="Thickness.None">0</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="Thickness.Hairline">1</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="Thickness.PopupPadding">10,7,10,7</Thickness>

    <GridLength x:Key="GridLength.Auto">Auto</GridLength>
    <GridLength x:Key="GridLength.Star">*</GridLength>
</ResourceDictionary>
